g.V().repeat(__.out()).times(2).path().by().by("name").by("lang") In group() a bare value by() collects the members of each key as a list, as TinkerPop's GroupStep does for an identity value traversal (map(identity).fold()), instead of keeping one member: g.V().group().by(T.label).by() maps person to its four vertices. Rust: by(__::identity()).

